interact/configuration-110","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#options-explained","content":"`\"hold\"` requires holding the key; `\"toggle\"` switches on/off per press."},"860":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-111","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#options-explained","content":"The `maxInteractDistance` directly affects performance. A lower value means fewer interactions are checked and rendered each frame."},"861":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-112","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#options-explained","content":"Set `hideWhenEmpty.models = true` if model targets should lose their marker when `canInteract` returns false. An option can set `hideWhenEmpty = true` or `false` to override the type default. The marker only hides when every option on the target wants to hide."},"862":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-113","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#options-explained","content":"Interact is registered as a FiveM keybind (`interact_action`). Players rebind it in GTA Settings → Key Bindings → FiveM. The prompt reads the live mapping, so the keycap updates after they leave the pause menu."},"863":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-114","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#distant-indicator","content":"`config.indicator` is the mark on targets that are in range but are not the open prompt. Set it to an id from the gallery. Click a name to copy it."},"864":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-115","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#distant-indicator","content":"The marker stays white. Its second color is the theme accent, or `config.themeColor` when that is set. Set `indicatorColors` to replace either color. Add a fourth number when that color should be translucent, such as `{ 255, 80, 40, 0.5 }` or `{ 255, 80, 40, 128 }`. `wedge` keeps its own whites until you set a color there."},"865":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-116","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#distant-indicator","content":"`indicatorScale` sizes every marker the same way."},"866":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-117","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#distant-indicator","content":"A custom marker is a file at `web/indicators/<id>.css` whose loader is a `<span class=\"loader\">`. `--color-1` is the first `indicatorColors` entry and `--color-2` is the second."},"867":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-118","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#themes","content":"`config.theme` selects the prompt skin. Each built-in look has its own accent in `config.themeColors`. Leave `config.themeColor` as `nil` unless you want one color on every theme."},"868":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-119","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#themes","content":"Id"},"869":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-120","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#themes","content":"Description"},"870":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-121","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#themes","content":"`legacy`"},"871":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-122","page_id":"/docs/interact/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/interact/configuration#themes","content":"Original prompt. Dark rows, Roboto, and a blue fill on the selected row"},"872":{"id":"/docs/interact/configuration-123","page_id":"/docs/interact/c