up-18","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","content":"These steps are **in addition** to defining your lootboxes in `config.lua`. You must also ensure the item definitions exist in your inventory/framework so players can hold and use the items."},"1710":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-19","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true` (the default), sleepless\\_lootbox automatically registers each lootbox as a usable item through the framework bridge. However, the item must still be **defined** in your inventory or framework's item list — the resource can only register the *use callback*, not create the item definition itself."},"1711":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-20","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#ox_core--ox_inventory-setup","content":"When using **ox\\_core**, usable items are handled through **ox\\_inventory** item definitions rather than the framework itself. For each lootbox case item, you need to add a `server.export` entry in your ox\\_inventory item definitions that points back to this resource."},"1712":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `ox_inventory/data/items.lua`:"},"1713":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"The `server.export` value **must** follow the format `sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>`, where `<item_name>` matches the lootbox key defined in your `config.lua` or registered via exports. Without this, using the item will do nothing."},"1714":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"ox\\_inventory sees that the item has a `server.export` defined."},"1715":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-24","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"When a player uses the item, ox\\_inventory calls the matching export on `sleepless_lootbox`."},"1716":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-25","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The ox framework bridge registers these exports automatically when `config.registerUsableItems = true`."},"1717":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-26","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1718":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-27","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for ox\\_inventory:"},"1719":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-28","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `server.export` — only the case items do."},"1720":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-29","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1721":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-30","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"When using **QBCore** or **Qbox**, lootbox case items must be defined in your shared items table with `useable = true`. This allows the framework to register usable item callbacks."},"1722":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-31","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `qb-core/shared/items.lua`:"},"1723":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-32","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"The `useable = true` flag is **required**. Without it, `QBCore.Functions.CreateUseableItem` (or `exports.qbx_core:CreateUseableItem` for Qbox) will not be able to register the callback, and using the item will do nothing."},"1724":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The framework sees that the item has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1725":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true`, the bridge calls `CreateUseableItem` for each lootbox."},"1726":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When a player uses the item, the framework triggers the registered callback."},"1727":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1728":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setu