ootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**ox\\_inventory:** Verify the item definition includes `server.export = \"sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>\"` and that the item name matches your lootbox key exactly."},"1735":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**QBCore/Qbox:** Verify the item definition has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1736":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**All frameworks:** Ensure `config.registerUsableItems = true` in your `config.lua`."},"1737":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**All frameworks:** Ensure `sleepless_lootbox` starts **after** your framework and inventory in `server.cfg`."},"1738":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#no-supported-framework-detected-warning","content":"Check that your framework resource is started before `sleepless_lootbox`. The bridge auto-detects the framework by checking if the resource is started, so load order matters."},"1739":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#lootbox-opens-but-no-item-is-given","content":"This is likely an inventory bridge issue. Make sure the loot content items (not the case items) are also defined in your inventory system. The resource can only give items that your inventory recognizes."},"1740":{"id":"/docs/lootbox","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"page","content":"Sleepless Lootbox","breadcrumbs":["Docs"