ting-47","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#dependencies","content":"No framework resource is required. On join, bucket state is published for ox\\_core, ESX, QBCore, and Qbox, and for any player who joins before those events fire."},"2447":{"id":"/docs/routing-48","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#download-the-resource-step","content":"Download a release from GitHub."},"2448":{"id":"/docs/routing-49","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#add-to-server-step","content":"Place the `sleepless_routing` folder in your server's resources directory. Keep the folder name so `exports.sleepless_routing` resolves."},"2449":{"id":"/docs/routing-50","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#configure-your-server-step","content":"Add the following to your `server.cfg`:"},"2450":{"id":"/docs/routing-51","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#open-a-named-instance-step","content":"`requestBucketId` creates the bucket the first time and returns the same id after that. The second argument is population. `false` keeps ambient peds and traffic out of the instance. The third argument is an optional lockdown mode (`inactive`, `relaxed`, `strict`, `no_dummy`, `full`). Leave it unset when something inside the instance spawns networked entities from the client. `strict` blocks those spawns."},"2451":{"id":"/docs/routing-52","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#open-a-named-instance-step","content":"Other players in the same vehicle move with the player. A later `setBucketOptions` call can change population or lockdown on a bucket that already exists. `getPlayersInBucket` returns whoever is in it right now. `triggerClientEventForBucket` sends one client event to those players through `lib.triggerClientEvent`."},"2452":{"id":"/docs/routing-53","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#open-a-named-instance-step","content":"`currentBucket` stays aligned when another resource moves the player with `SetPlayerRoutingBucket`. The state bag updates from `onPlayerBucketChange`."},"2453":{"id":"/docs/routing-54","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#clusters","content":"A cluster is a name for several buckets. It does not move players. Use it when one client event, or one player list, should cover more than one instance."},"2454":{"id":"/docs/routing-55","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#clusters","content":"`createCluster` registers the name. `addBucketToCluster` takes a bucket id or a registered name and stores the numeric id. The same bucket can sit in more than one cluster. Adding it again is a no-op. `getClusterBuckets` returns those ids in the order they were added. `getPlayersInCluster` reads each player's live routing bucket, so a player moved by another resource is included when their current bucket is in the group."},"2455":{"id":"/docs/routing-56","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#clusters","content":"`triggerClientEventForCluster` uses the same argument order as `lib.triggerClientEvent`: event name, then the cluster name, then the payload. An empty cluster still returns `true`."},"2456":{"id":"/docs/routing-57","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#clusters","content":"`removeCluster` forgets the group only. `removeBucketId` does not take a bucket out of a cluster. After that name is gone, remove the member with its numeric id."},"2457":{"id":"/docs/routing-58","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#debug","content":"`/setroute` is registered only when `debug` is true in `config.lua`. It requires the `command` permission. With no argument, the player returns to the global bucket. With a name, they move into that named bucket (population off)."},"2458":{"id":"/docs/routing-59","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#debug","content":"`versionCheckEnabled` checks GitHub for a newer release when the resource starts. Leave it `true` unless the server has no outbound access."},"2459":{"id":"/docs/routing-60","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#support","content":"Discord"},"2460":{"id":"/docs/routing-61","page_id":"/docs/routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/routing#support","content":"GitHub Issues"},"2461":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","type":"page","content":"Configuration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Free Resources","Waypoints"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/waypoints/configuration"},"2462":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration-0","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/waypoints/configuration#map-waypoint-sync","content":"Map Waypoint Sync"},"2463":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration-1","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/waypoints/configuration#default-waypoint-settings","content":"Default Waypoint Settings"},"2464":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration-2","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/waypoints/configuration#dui-settings","content":"DUI Settings"},"2465":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration-3","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/waypoints/configuration#rendering-settings","content":"Rendering Settings"},"2466":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration-4","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/waypoints/configuration#timers","content":"Timers"},"2467":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration-5","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/waypoints/configuration#server-settings","content":"Server Settings"},"2468":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/configuration-6",