waypoints/timers#timer-data","content":"`showLabel` and `showValue` only hide text. The bar, ring, dots, and other fills stay. Chip and stack are only those two texts, so hiding both leaves an empty plate."},"2857":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-103","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#duration-timer","content":"`onEnd` runs on the client that created the timer, before the plate is removed. The local event still fires after it, which is useful when another resource needs to hear about every timer."},"2858":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-104","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#duration-timer","content":"`updateTimer` changes only the fields you pass. Passing `duration` starts that timer over. Passing `progress` on a duration timer jumps the fill."},"2859":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-105","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#duration-timer","content":"`colors` replaces that flat colour. Leave `blend` out, or set it `false`, and the fill switches the moment progress reaches a stop. `blend = true` holds the current colour, then eases into the next one on the way into the stop. Pass `colors = {}` to `updateTimer` to go back to `color`."},"2860":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-106","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#duration-timer","content":"Set `removeOnComplete` to `false` if the plate should stay full until you remove it. `onEnd` and the ended event still run."},"2861":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-107","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#duration-timer","content":"`onEnd` does not cross the network. A timer created on the server still fires `sleepless_waypoints:client:timerEnded` on each client that has it. Keep the reward on the server with your own timeout, the same way the example below removes the timer."},"2862":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-108","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#script-timer","content":"Leave `duration` out and set `progress` whenever your script moves."},"2863":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-109","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#script-timer","content":"Script timers do not end on their own. Remove them when the action is done."},"2864":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-110","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#server","content":"`source` can be one player id, a list of ids, or `-1` for everyone online. The id you get back is the server id. Use it with `updateTimer` and `removeTimer` on the server. It is not the id the client uses locally."},"2865":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-111","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#server","content":"`removeAllTimers()` drops every server timer. `removeAllTimers(playerId)` drops timers that were aimed at that one player. Global timers stay up for everyone else."},"2866":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-112","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#server","content":"A player who joins after you create a timer does not receive it. Each client runs the countdown from the moment the timer arrives, and each client fires `sleepless_waypoints:client:timerEnded` on its own. If the server created the timer, remove it there when the interaction is over."},"2867":{"id":"/docs/waypoints/timers-113","page_id":"/docs/waypoints/timers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/waypoints/timers#server","content":"Client exports are documented on Client. Server exports are documented on Server. Defaults live in Configuration."},"2868":{"id":"/docs/crafting/Events/Client","page_id":"/docs/crafting/Events/Client","type":"page","content":"Client Events","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Paid 